# CANONICAL MAPPING LAYER (THE BRIDGE THAT MAKES COMPUNDING LEARNING REAL)

## 1) Affect mapping → universal pressure scores

Each vertical emotion group maps to the universal lattice:

| Vertical       | +3        | +1           | 0           | −1             | −3          |
| -------------- | --------- | ------------ | ----------- | -------------- | ----------- |
| Healthcare     | Trust     | Reassurance  | Uncertainty | Anxiety        | Fear        |
| Fraud/Security | Relief    | Confidence   | Uncertainty | Alarm          | Panic       |
| Insurance      | Relief    | Satisfaction | Ambivalence | Frustration    | Desperation |
| Retail/E-Com   | Delight   | Satisfaction | Ambivalence | Disappointment | Anger       |
| SaaS/Tech      | Empowered | Satisfied    | Neutral     | Frustrated     | Blocked     |

**Canonical query becomes possible:**

* “Show me all −3 pressure experiences across the enterprise, regardless of vertical language.”

---

## 2) Intent mapping → 7 universal speech acts

Every vertical intent label must map to one of:

* Compliment / Complaint / Request / Suggestion / Question / Usage Insight / Emerging Trend

This makes the OU engine stable across domains:

* same routing rules
* same thresholds
* same clustering expectations

---

## 3) Action mapping → 4 universal strategic classes

Every vertical action label maps to:

* Fix / Optimize / Amplify / Innovate

This enables cross-vertical operational learning:

* “When pressure is −3, what action class historically yields the best ERI delta?”

